**Definition 3.1 (One common dual form and its coefficients).** Let
$C\in M_3(\mathbb R)$, $y\in\mathbb R^3$ and
$(\delta_\nu)_{\nu\in\mathcal N}\in\mathbb R^6$ be arbitrary.
In the event application of §5 these are obtained from one common
event-multiplier tuple and all three TP multipliers. Define

$$
\mathcal B_{C,y,\delta}(a)=
\sum_j\left(\|a\|^2y_j-\sum_iC_{ij}h_i(a)\right)H_j
-\frac12\sum_\nu\delta_\nu\sum_{k=1}^2z_{\nu k}(a)F_{\nu k}.
\tag{3.1}
$$

The notation $\mathcal B$ distinguishes this five-by-five quadratic
matrix form from the spectral matrix $B=-A^2$. For $p_i\ge0$, set

$$
\begin{gathered}
\ell_j(p)=\frac{y_j\sum_ip_i-\sum_iC_{ij}p_i/\sqrt{n_i}}
                 {\sqrt{n_j}},\qquad
L_{jk}=\frac{y_j}{\sqrt{n_j}}-\frac{C_{kj}}{\sqrt{n_kn_j}},\\
A_0(p)=\ell_0(p),\quad
A_+(p)=\ell_+(p)-\delta_{2+}p_+/4,\quad
A_-(p)=\ell_-(p)-\delta_{2-}p_-/4,\\
B_+(p)=\ell_+(p)+\delta_{2+}p_+/4,\qquad
B_-(p)=\ell_-(p)+\delta_{2-}p_-/4,\\
A_i(p)=\sum_k\alpha_{ik}p_k,\quad B_j(p)=\sum_k\beta_{jk}p_k,\\
\alpha_{0k}=L_{0k},\quad
\alpha_{+k}=L_{+k}-\tfrac14\delta_{2+}\mathbf1_{k=+},\quad
\alpha_{-k}=L_{-k}-\tfrac14\delta_{2-}\mathbf1_{k=-},\\
\beta_{+k}=L_{+k}+\tfrac14\delta_{2+}\mathbf1_{k=+},\qquad
\beta_{-k}=L_{-k}+\tfrac14\delta_{2-}\mathbf1_{k=-}.
\end{gathered}
\tag{3.2}
$$

Use the signed scalars

$$
u=\delta_+/2,\qquad v=\delta_-/2,\qquad
w=(\delta_\Delta+\delta_\Sigma)/4,\qquad
t=(\delta_\Delta-\delta_\Sigma)/4,
\tag{3.3}
$$

and write $c_{0+}=u,c_{0-}=v,c_{+-}=w$. In ordered bases
$(d,u_+,u_-)$ and $(v_+,v_-)$ define

$$
\begin{aligned}
\mathcal R(p)&=\begin{pmatrix}
A_0&-u\sqrt{p_0p_+}&-v\sqrt{p_0p_-}\\
-u\sqrt{p_0p_+}&A_+&-w\sqrt{p_+p_-}\\
-v\sqrt{p_0p_-}&-w\sqrt{p_+p_-}&A_-
\end{pmatrix},\\
\mathcal T(p)&=\begin{pmatrix}
B_+&-t\sqrt{p_+p_-}\\
-t\sqrt{p_+p_-}&B_-
\end{pmatrix},\\
\mathscr F(p)&=A_0A_+A_-
 -A_0w^2p_+p_--A_+v^2p_0p_--A_-u^2p_0p_+
 -2uvw\,p_0p_+p_-.
\end{aligned}
\tag{3.4}
$$

All $A_i,B_j$ in (3.4) are evaluated at that same $p$.
$\mathscr F$ is a homogeneous ternary cubic. No sign is assumed
for $u,v,w,t$.

